# Intentionally empty of directives.
#
# History: this file used to try to block PHP execution in this folder
# at the Apache level. First with <FilesMatch> + Require all denied /
# Order+Deny (needs the Limit/AuthConfig AllowOverride classes) - that
# 500'd on this exact live host for every request under this folder
# (confirmed 2026-09-24: opening a real uploaded thumbnail URL returned
# the host's own ".htaccess error" page). Replaced with RemoveHandler/
# RemoveType (needs only FileInfo) on the assumption that class was
# permitted here since RewriteRule elsewhere on this host needs it too -
# that assumption was wrong: re-tested live and RemoveHandler/RemoveType
# 500'd exactly the same way. This host's AllowOverride is evidently
# stricter than either attempt could satisfy, so the only version of
# this file guaranteed not to 500 here is one with no directives at all.
#
# This is NOT a security gap. PHP execution was never the primary
# defense for this folder - UploadController::store() already refuses
# any file whose extension isn't on an explicit image/video/audio/doc
# whitelist (upload_extension_allowed()) AND whose actual content
# doesn't match that extension (upload_content_matches_extension()),
# and every saved filename is server-generated (uniqid()-based), never
# the uploader's own filename or extension choice. A .php file can
# never be saved into this folder in the first place - there is nothing
# left here for an .htaccess-level block to additionally protect
# against.
